# Line endings — fix wave 2026-11-20, package `line-endings`.
#
# This Windows machine checks out with core.autocrlf=true, and git config must
# never be changed, so the policy lives in this file instead: text files are
# stored with LF in the repository AND written to the working tree with LF on
# every machine (Windows, macOS, Linux). Gates that compare exact bytes depend
# on this — the functions unit suite reads firestore.rules and other source
# files, and the rules-file hash pins drift if a checkout converts them.
#
# `text=auto` still normalises every other text file to LF in the repository;
# the explicit `eol=lf` lines below remove the platform-default checkout so
# `core.autocrlf=true` cannot put CRLF into source, config, docs or rules.

* text=auto

# Source
*.ts  text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js  text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Config and data
*.json   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.gradle text eol=lf

# Docs and markup
*.md   text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf

# Security rules
*.rules text eol=lf

# Attribute files
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Binaries are never converted: images, fonts, keystores, jar/aar, apk/aab.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.bmp   binary
*.avif  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.eot   binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks   binary
*.p12   binary
*.pfx   binary
*.jar   binary
*.aar   binary
*.apk   binary
*.aab   binary

# Pre-existing root artifact committed before any line-ending policy: its blob
# contains CRLF (double-CR) bytes, so forcing text eol=lf would rewrite the
# committed blob. This package forbids renormalisation, so it stays untouched.
LOOP_PROMPT_120.md -text
